import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Community programs | The Common's history" description="How The Common has supported Squamish entrepreneurs, local groups, and nonprofit events through desk space, grants, and venue sponsorship.">
  <header class="page-hd"><div class="wrap"><h1>Making room for other people's ideas.</h1><p>The original Common Capital, community grant, and venue sponsorship programs grew from a simple question: who could do more with this space if cost were less of a barrier?</p></div></header>
  <section class="section light"><div class="wrap programs-intro"><p>Peter built The Common to make stronger connections between people and organizations in Squamish. The programs below were ways to put that idea to work. They are described here as part of The Common's history. Funding, discounts, and free venue use are not confirmed current offers.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section warm"><div class="wrap program-list">
    <article><span>01 · Desk space</span><h2>Common Capital</h2><p>This program drew on the idea of social capital that inspired The Common. A person with time, useful skills, or good connections could contribute to the community in exchange for more accessible desk space. Peter especially wanted to hear from people working on innovation, environmental sustainability, Indigenous equity, human rights, and community building.</p></article>
    <article><span>02 · Local groups</span><h2>Community grants</h2><p>The Common worked with Community Futures to help Squamish groups run meetups and events around small business, entrepreneurship, technology, outdoor recreation, and the green economy. The original grant page described support for venue rental, marketing, and promotion, with funding of up to $1,000 at that time.</p></article>
    <article><span>03 · A place to gather</span><h2>Venue sponsorship</h2><p>Peter also wanted local charities and community groups to be able to meet, fundraise, and show films without a venue bill stopping the idea. The original program described nonprofit pricing, free rentals for some community groups, and a profit share option for some events.</p></article>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section light"><div class="wrap program-close"><h2>Tell us what you're planning.</h2><p>These historical programs explain the spirit behind the space. If you're organizing something for Squamish, send us the details and we'll tell you what is possible now.</p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a><a class="inline-link" href="/community/">Back to the community</a></div></section>
</Base>
<style>.programs-intro{max-width:850px}.programs-intro p,.program-list p,.program-close p{color:var(--muted);font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.8}.program-list{display:grid;gap:2rem}.program-list article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(130px,.4fr) minmax(180px,.7fr) minmax(0,1.5fr);gap:2rem;border-top:2px solid var(--forest);padding-top:2rem}.program-list span{color:var(--forest);font-size:.82rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}.program-list h2{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.6rem);margin:0}.program-list p{margin:0}.program-close{max-width:850px}.program-close h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,3.4vw,3rem);margin:.7rem 0}.program-close .btn{margin:1rem 1.5rem 0 0}@media(max-width:760px){.program-list article{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.7rem}}</style>
